WEBVTT

00:00:16.248 --> 00:00:19.375
It's too late.
Grindelwald has come for Credence.

00:00:21.337 --> 00:00:24.005
- He might already have him.
- It's not too late.

00:00:24.089 --> 00:00:25.673
We can still get to him first.

00:00:28.135 --> 00:00:29.219
Where are you going?

00:00:29.678 --> 00:00:31.179
The French Ministry of Magic.

00:00:31.347 --> 00:00:33.264
That's the last place Credence would go.

00:00:33.432 --> 00:00:35.600
There's a box
hidden in the Ministry, Tina.

00:00:36.352 --> 00:00:38.353
It's a box that can tell us
who Credence really is.

00:00:38.521 --> 00:00:40.772
A box? What are you talking about?

00:00:41.023 --> 00:00:42.023
Trust me.

00:00:45.653 --> 00:00:47.987
CREDENCE: You wanna come out,
just for a little while?

00:00:48.072 --> 00:00:49.489
You can be free.

00:00:51.826 --> 00:00:53.243
(BABY BIRD CHIRPING)

00:00:58.290 --> 00:00:59.290
NAGINI: Credence.

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:04.671
(SHUSHING)

00:01:07.842 --> 00:01:08.842
What do you want?

00:01:08.926 --> 00:01:09.926
GRINDELWALD: From you?

00:01:11.345 --> 00:01:12.345
Nothing.

00:01:15.266 --> 00:01:16.349
For you?

00:01:18.394 --> 00:01:20.228
Everything I never had.

00:01:21.438 --> 00:01:24.524
But what is it you want, my boy?

00:01:25.442 --> 00:01:27.193
I want to know who I am.

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:41.708
This is where you will find proof
of your true identity.

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:51.175
Come to Père Lachaise tonight,
and you will discover the truth.

00:01:53.971 --> 00:01:55.388
(GRINDELWALD DISAPPEARING)

00:02:08.527 --> 00:02:10.528
Father, why did you make me...

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:14.240
JACOB: Wait...

00:02:15.993 --> 00:02:17.410
(GASPS) Wait.

00:02:17.494 --> 00:02:18.578
(CLEARING THROAT)

00:02:22.124 --> 00:02:23.958
(STOMACH RUMBLING)

00:02:38.849 --> 00:02:41.476
I'm afraid we keep no food in the house.

00:02:43.562 --> 00:02:45.021
(STAMMERS) Are you a ghost?

00:02:45.189 --> 00:02:46.272
No.

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:49.317
No. I'm alive.

00:02:50.444 --> 00:02:53.321
But I'm an alchemist
and therefore immortal.

00:02:55.157 --> 00:02:57.283
You don't look a day over 375.

00:02:58.243 --> 00:02:59.744
(ALCHEMIST CHUCKLES)

00:03:00.746 --> 00:03:02.372
I'm sorry that we didn't knock.

00:03:02.539 --> 00:03:04.374
No. No matter.

00:03:04.541 --> 00:03:06.793
Albus told me some friends
might be dropping in.

00:03:07.836 --> 00:03:09.295
Nicolas Flamel.

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:12.090
Oh.

00:03:13.175 --> 00:03:14.258
Jacob Kowalski.

00:03:14.343 --> 00:03:15.385
- (BONE CRACKS)
- Oh!

00:03:17.012 --> 00:03:18.054
I'm sorry.

00:03:18.138 --> 00:03:19.138
It's all right.

00:03:19.223 --> 00:03:21.641
- I didn't...
- Oh... Oh!

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:27.897
(PANTING)

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:35.071
At last, we see some development.

00:03:35.155 --> 00:03:37.657
Yeah. I've seen one of these before.

00:03:37.741 --> 00:03:39.867
(CLEARS THROAT) It was at the fair.

00:03:40.077 --> 00:03:41.661
There was this dame there,
and she had a veil,

00:03:41.745 --> 00:03:45.039
and I gave her a nickel,
and she told me about my future.

00:03:45.666 --> 00:03:48.584
And she missed out
on quite a bit, actually.

00:03:52.089 --> 00:03:53.756
Oh. Hey, hey.

00:03:55.092 --> 00:03:57.427
Wait a minute, I know him.
That's the kid. That's Credence.

00:04:00.222 --> 00:04:01.222
Jeez.

00:04:02.933 --> 00:04:04.392
Hey... Hey!

00:04:05.728 --> 00:04:08.187
That's Queenie. There she is. Hi, baby.

00:04:08.689 --> 00:04:10.857
Where is this? Is this here?

00:04:10.941 --> 00:04:13.401
Yes. This is the Lestrange tomb.

00:04:13.569 --> 00:04:16.070
It lies in the cemetery
of Père Lachaise.

00:04:17.364 --> 00:04:19.073
I'm coming, baby. Stay right there.

00:04:19.241 --> 00:04:20.491
Thank you, Mr. Flamel.

00:04:20.659 --> 00:04:24.203
- Ouch.
- I'm sorry. I'm sorry. Okay.

00:04:24.371 --> 00:04:27.373
Oh, look after Mr. Tentacles for me.
Oh, no.

00:04:27.541 --> 00:04:28.541
I'm sorry. I gotta go.

00:04:28.625 --> 00:04:30.043
FLAMEL: Please,
you mustn't go to the cemetery.

00:04:48.645 --> 00:04:49.812
(EXCLAIMS IN FRENCH)

00:04:52.316 --> 00:04:53.316
(GASPS)

00:04:53.525 --> 00:04:54.734
What's happening?

00:04:54.902 --> 00:04:56.527
FLAMEL: Exactly what he said
would happen.

00:04:57.821 --> 00:05:00.073
Grindelwald rallies
at the cemetery tonight,

00:05:00.157 --> 00:05:01.574
and there will be death.

00:05:01.742 --> 00:05:02.825
Then you gotta go.

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:05.620
What? I haven't seen action
in 200 years.

00:05:05.788 --> 00:05:08.581
Flamel, you can do this.
We believe in you.

00:05:17.883 --> 00:05:20.051
The box is in
the Ancestral Records room, Tina.

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:21.636
So it's three floors down.

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:22.762
Is that Polyjuice?

00:05:22.930 --> 00:05:24.639
It's just enough to get me inside.

00:05:27.101 --> 00:05:28.518
(NEWT GROANING)

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:35.399
- Who...
- It's my brother, Theseus.

00:05:35.943 --> 00:05:38.736
He's an Auror and a hugger.

00:05:40.948 --> 00:05:42.115
What's happening?

00:05:42.282 --> 00:05:43.324
Grindelwald's rallying.

00:05:43.408 --> 00:05:45.034
We don't know where,
but we think it's tonight.

00:05:49.748 --> 00:05:51.374
- Be careful.
- Of course.

00:05:51.542 --> 00:05:53.626
- Promise me you'll be careful.
- Of course. I'm gonna be careful.

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:56.796
Listen, I want you to hear this from me.

00:05:56.964 --> 00:05:58.965
They think that Credence boy
might be your missing brother.

00:05:59.049 --> 00:06:00.591
- My brother is dead.
- I know.

00:06:00.759 --> 00:06:02.093
- He died.
- I know.

00:06:02.261 --> 00:06:04.887
- How many times, Theseus?
- And the records will prove that.

00:06:05.556 --> 00:06:08.891
- Okay? They can't lie.
- Theseus.

00:06:14.606 --> 00:06:17.441
I want every person at that rally
arrested. If they resist...

00:06:17.609 --> 00:06:18.901
Sir, forgive me, but if we go in
too heavy,

00:06:18.986 --> 00:06:21.195
- don't we run the risk of adding to...
- Just do it.

00:06:39.047 --> 00:06:41.507
I don't suppose you can Disapparate
on Ministry premises in France, can you?

00:06:41.675 --> 00:06:42.675
Nope.

00:06:43.135 --> 00:06:45.094
(GRUNTING) Pity.

00:06:46.054 --> 00:06:48.139
- Newt!
- Yes, I know. I know it's...

00:06:49.224 --> 00:06:51.142
(ANNOUNCEMENT IN FRENCH ON PA)

00:06:52.811 --> 00:06:53.811
THESEUS: Newt!

00:06:55.314 --> 00:06:56.314
Newt!

00:06:56.523 --> 00:06:58.065
- Oh!
- That's your brother?

00:06:58.150 --> 00:06:59.609
So I think I may have mentioned
in my letters

00:06:59.776 --> 00:07:00.860
that we have quite
a complicated relationship.

00:07:00.944 --> 00:07:02.236
Newt, stop!

00:07:02.404 --> 00:07:03.613
- Does he wanna kill you?
- Frequently.

00:07:04.823 --> 00:07:05.907
Enough!

00:07:12.789 --> 00:07:14.415
He needs to control his temper.

00:07:14.583 --> 00:07:15.875
(GRUNTING)

00:07:19.588 --> 00:07:21.839
I think that might have been
the best moment of my life.

